{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789291979,"nonce":"nFEmRrnVKg+nB9Tzz2jSZFmTWis=","title":"Baseline compile of a Num-guarded recursive function with other calls fails the Cranelift verifier","message":"A function whose parameters are all guarded Num and which calls itself (bench/ash/binary_trees.wren bottomUpTree) is lowered a second time as an inner f64 body; that body carries its parameters raw, and any other call in it (TreeNode.new here) is handed the raw f64 where the helper expects a boxed Value: 'arg 4 (v0) has type f64, expected i64'. The compile fails, the function never leaves the interpreter, and ash/binary_trees ran at 6.3 s instead of 2.8 s on the Mac. Reproduce with WLIFT_JIT_DEBUG=1 on the bench. Fix: the inner body is only built when the recursion is the body's only call.","files":null}]}